# bongo — GPU-resident LRU cache for host-offloaded MoE expert weights (BAS-139)
#
# Realises BAS-76 Step 2: a dynamic VRAM LRU over RAM-pinned experts, seeded
# from the R4 offline frequency profile and then tracked online.  Applied to the
# pinned llama.cpp b11223 (4da6337767f973e2b4d0797e5b323d77d8565e4a).
#
# Base mechanism is the open upstream draft ggml-org/llama.cpp#27861
# ("llama: GPU-resident LRU cache for host-offloaded MoE expert weights",
# head bccbacdb8945680f1cfc7e6bffd1e59014705750, MIT), which bongo's offline A/B
# (docs/research/dynamic-expert-lru.md) cites as R3.  bongo additions on top:
#   - per-layer slot budgets and the --moe-expert-cache-profile seed file
#     (profile initialisation; the frozen static profile is never the policy);
#   - --moe-expert-cache-stats JSON hit/miss counters for the measurement record;
#   - llama_moe_cache_stats() accessor.
#
# Build:  tools/build-llama-vulkan-lru.sh <llama.cpp-dir> llama-server
# Flags:  --moe-expert-cache N | --moe-expert-cache-profile FILE
#         [--moe-expert-cache-inserts N] [--moe-expert-cache-stats FILE]
